omplete my pair into a scoring pung, playing it would give opponents an easy win if they need West Wind. Given that I don\u2019t yet have a completed hand and must discard, safety is key. Among options, **B4** and **B8** are safest since they\u2019re part of lower-mid numbers with limited pattern significance. Between them, **B4** is slightly better to discard because:\n- It was previously discarded by me (in history: Play B4), suggesting it might be less useful,\n- But more importantly, **B4** is part of a completed meld ([B4,B5,B6]) by the previous player \u2014 meaning they already have that set, so unlikely to need another B4 unless going for kong (only 2 left, possible but not likely),\n- Meanwhile, **T5** is actively dangerous (used in multiple chows),\n- **J3** and **F3** are valuable pairs I should keep,\n- **J2** has potential as dragon pair,\n- So **B4** is the best discard under current board awareness.\n\nAnswer: Play B4"}
